#
# BIND-9a (D-BIND-141, D-BIND-149): the linux-x64 shim's platform floors, in one place.
# scripts/check_shim_dependencies.sh requires the shim's highest GLIBC_ and GLIBCXX_
# symbol versions to EQUAL these, and scripts/check_dotnet_packages.sh requires the
# package README to state them; so a build-image change that moves a floor fails both
# until this file and dotnet/README.package.md are changed with it. GLIBC_FLOOR moved from 2.38
# to 2.34 with Fast DDS 3.4.3 (BIND-9b-7, D-BIND-169), ConanCenter's prebuilt binary; the C++
# runtime (GLIBCXX_3.4.32, GCC 13) is the binding floor, so the supported distros did not move.
#
# BIND-9b-7 (D-BIND-172): the floors are the build profiles'. GLIBCXX_FLOOR is the C++ runtime of
# the compiler .conan-profiles/Linux-gcc13-x86_64-Release names (GCC 13 -> GLIBCXX_3.4.32; GCC 14
# would be 3.4.33), so moving that profile fails the measured-equals-stated check until this file
# moves with it. GLIBC_FLOOR is not a profile setting: it is what the build machine's headers and
# ConanCenter's prebuilt dependencies make it, so it stays measured. The win-x64 floor, the
# redistributable 14.40, is the toolset of .conan-profiles/Windows-msvc194-x86_64-Release
# (compiler.version=194), stated in the package README and the loader's message.
GLIBC_FLOOR=2.34
GLIBCXX_FLOOR=3.4.32
